        "original_id": "675711e8-d363-51c3-9b2a-95469da09e31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steve Perry, Dennis Lyxzén, Jonathan Cain\n- Bands: Journey, Refused, INVSN\n- Songs and Albums: “After the Fall”, Frontiers\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Perry was the lead singer of Journey during the band's most commercially successful periods from 1977 to 1987 and again from 1995 to 1998.\n- Dennis Lyxzén was born on June 19, 1972, in Umeå, Sweden.\n- Dennis Lyxzén is best known as the lead vocalist for the Swedish hardcore punk band Refused.\n- In 1983, Jonathan Cain and Steve Perry wrote “After the Fall” for the album Frontiers.\n- “After the Fall” was the third single released from the 1983 album Frontiers.\n- Dennis Lyxzén is currently the vocalist in INVSN.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
